## 1. Objective restatement (traceability)

Produce `reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md`: for ≥3 real sealed goals from
`reviews/tasks/`, a hand-extraction attempt into the SAEOS-1 §4.3 node types recording
per-field `extractable` / `partial` / `absent`, plus an explicit `GO` / `NO-GO` verdict with the
loss ratio.

Acceptance (verbatim from `backlog/SAKG-1-backlog.yaml`, node `S-PROBE`, `accept:`):

```
A1  test -f reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
A2  rg -q '^verdict: (GO|NO-GO)$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
A3  test $(rg -c '^## goal: ' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md) -ge 3
A4  rg -q '^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$' reviews/spikes/sakg-s1-extraction-probe.md
```

The analytical content is **already frozen** by the DESIGN stage (artifact `cd396700eee7`,
455 lines, `verdict: GO`, `loss_ratio: 0.39`, four `## goal:` sections covering B0.0, B0.1,
B0.2, B0.4). This plan does not re-open, re-score, or re-verdict that analysis. It plans the
transcription of the frozen body to its canonical path, its verification, and its rollback.

**Sample-size note (not a deviation).** The objective says "3 real sealed goals (e.g. B0.0,
B0.1, B0.2)"; the DESIGN sampled **four**, adding B0.4. A3 requires `-ge 3`, so four satisfies
it. The fourth is load-bearing, not surplus: DESIGN §9 states the verdict is stable under
excluding B0.4 (loss 0.45) and under excluding B0.2 (loss 0.35). Dropping to exactly three
would destroy that stability argument. **WU-2 must carry all four.**

