**Plan-time finding (recommendation only, CER-5 — not actioned here).** Acceptance command A4,
`^loss_ratio: 0\.[0-9]+$`, admits only the form `0.NN`. A probe measuring a loss ratio of
exactly `0` or `1.0` would produce a *correct* result that **fails its own gate**. This does not
affect the present run (`0.39` matches, E-P2), and the `accept:` list is frozen backlog content
that this plan has no authority to edit. Recorded so it can be raised at `G-S1-GO` and fixed in
`T-ROUNDTRIP`, whose oracle (`--assert-loss-ratio 0`) expects exactly the value A4 rejects.

